-- title:
--   Complete cardinality-layer enumeration with an internally built power table
-- statement:
--   Let $L,k\in\mathbb N$ with $k\le L+1$, and let $N=\binom{L}{k}$. Assume $D+N\le F$, $F+L+1\le\mathrm{space}\le\mathrm{word}$, $2^{L+1}\le\mathrm{word}$, and $d+L+1\le\mathrm{depth}$. The program must contain the setup, power-table and recursive layer-enumeration bodies.
--
--   Define the work count $E(L,k)=1$ when $k=0$ or $k>L$; otherwise let $E(L,k)=1+E(L-1,k)+E(L-1,k-1)+\binom{L}{k}$. The call with $(L,k,D,F)$ terminates within $17L+65+150E(L,k)$ steps and satisfies
--   $$
--   r=N,\qquad \nu(D+i)=\operatorname{enumerateLayer}(L,k)_i\quad(i<N),\qquad
--   \nu(F+j)=2^j\quad(j\le L).
--   $$
--   The output lists exactly the masks with $k$ set bits in recursive lower-half-first order. Cells below $F$ outside $[D,D+N)$ are preserved.
--
--   This gives a complete layer enumerator with its lookup table constructed internally.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightSubsetEnumerationSetup.lean#L23-L66

